   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «Abba Shaul says: Also» among those who have no share in the World-to-Come is «one who pronounces the» ineffable «name» of God as it is written, «with its letters.» It is «taught» in a baraita: This is referring to one who pronounces the name «in the outlying areas» outside the Temple, «and in colloquial [aga] language,» for no particular purpose."
